  "note": "No Lean statement of (5.24); the first Euler factor is evaluated numerically or compared with τ(d)/d, and nothing on the main line needs it. Erratum: The footnote to (5.24) says the case y_i = sqrt x was checked with the stronger numerator 1-3x^3; that inequality is false for x > 0.57092 (e.g. X=0.6, y1=sqrt 0.6, y2=0.6: 1.5631 > 1.4249), so the described check does not cover the stated range 0 < x < 1 (checked by `scripts/checks/eq_5_24.py`)."
